<p>President Donald Trump told CNN in a phone interview Friday that Cuba is “gonna fall pretty soon,” arguing the island “want to make a deal so badly,” while stressing that his administration’s immediate focus remains the war against Iran. He also floated putting Secretary of State Marco Rubio in charge of Cuba-related efforts, saying, “I’m going to put Marco over there”. The comments widened the White House’s rhetoric beyond the Middle East and toward Latin America. Several outlets framed them as a sign Trump could shift more attention to Cuba after Iran. El País reported that Trump called the Iran war “doing very well militarily” and said he saw no deal to end it “except unconditional surrender”. Trump cast his Cuba remarks as the start of a possible deal, but the reporting offers few details on what any Cuba push would include—or whether any concrete diplomatic steps are already underway.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ylttw5zlMuL8w1kmNz6ncPZSYCjz8OnzwU5bjAaK5Skl2iqmr39SJCffgi4pNwHGa6bSGGnJYTUhMyg770OgIf5xdWmbnEvW8axVo040LriEynECe43iGno_5k02chaAm5Gupud8MbRyb6Sj8hgYmGvjmJ49ytxDCpQDdsa8TUedmVRuLFUI5p7rwHeDlyH6OTjAlGWHdFP6gPcik_i79O4B9AIC5WrGS424_e4' alt='Donald Trump at the White House, as pictured by El País.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Context (SCMP): SCMP said Cuba is &quot;crippled by a US energy blockade,&quot; and quoted Trump saying &quot;Cuba&#x27;s ready — after 50 years&quot; as he framed the island as a next agenda item after Iran.</li><li>Wider agenda: AllSides’ roundup of Politico reporting said Trump also talked about helping choose Iran’s next leader, predicted the Cuban regime’s downfall, and criticized Ukraine’s president while facing domestic backlash.</li></ul><blockquote>Cuba is gonna fall pretty soon. They want to make a deal so badly. - Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He told CNN that Cuba would “fall pretty soon,” said Cuba “want to make a deal,” and suggested putting Secretary 